  "findings": [
    "Before repair, the existing React-language fixture and external registered-root query fail under an actual Windows 8.3 TEMP parent; four other selected CI cases already pass locally.",
    "Host-selected registered-root aliases are rebuilt from current host inputs, never serialized into session authority and never resolved from arbitrary requested paths. Removal and Unicode lowercase-expansion refusals are tested.",
    "The React fixture compares decoded file paths for equivalent tilde URI spellings and uses the requested document independently of notification order. Production URI encoding and language IDs are unchanged.",
    "The console fixture calls the real kernel GetConsoleWindow through an owned compiled native probe, without a PowerShell CodeDOM dependency. Existing process flags are unchanged.",
    "Positive REPL/source-binding fixtures separate host/store/worker setup from unchanged 20-second operation budgets. The positive HTTP session fixture has a usable five-second absolute lifetime; short stalled-initialization expiry tests remain unchanged.",
    "The first frozen run also reproduces a reset before a complete oversized-header refusal. Production HTTP shutdown now half-closes the response and discards at most 16 KiB for at most 50ms within the original physical deadline, never parsing or dispatching tail bytes.",
    "Real TCP regressions prove bounded tail bytes, unchanged queued bytes after expiry/stop, and idle-peer deadline behavior. Existing framing, TLS, revocation, cancellation and absolute session lifetime tests remain active.",
    "The Unix positive archive CLI fixture now explicitly grants existing SQLite registry coordination; the default remains denied. Actual Unix validation of that fixture awaits CI."
  ],
  "preparationNotes": [
    "The first manual root-alias assertions expected file strings instead of public file objects; assertions were corrected to inspect path fields.",
    "The first frozen run retains two Clippy collapsible-if errors and one HTTP admission-response reset. It is not accepted.",
    "A separate three-test TCP preparation passed; its integration target matched zero tests due to the unit filter. Final validation executes the entire integration target."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Final native counts cover selected library/Session/HTTP/process/registry targets, not all Cargo targets; all scoped/diagnostic runs overlap and are not summed.",
    "TypeScript checks ran in r1; the explicit inter-run source delta contains only native Rust/test files, and no TypeScript inputs changed.",
    "The original hosted d4 Windows six failures are not declared fixed remotely merely because the six selected local short-temp cases pass.",
    "Unix host-install availability, macOS PDF/runtime/SQL issues, other STATUS/R1-R9 work, full-native acceptance and external provider installations remain open.",
    "No release, main merge, deployment or live GitHub App installation is claimed."
  ],
